(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/main.asl#" :text "Entry of site.wasm: the exports the DOM bridge (web/bridge/boot.js) calls. A wasm32 program cannot read a clock, so the bridge times render and hands the numbers to measured.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/main.asl#update" :text "Delivers message code to aslSite/app/update step with the model the bridge holds, prints the resulting bridge ops and returns the next model.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/main.asl#render" :text "Renders the home document with placeholder stats and returns its byte length; the bridge calls it twice to time a cold and a warm pass.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/main.asl#measured" :text "Prints the ops that show the bridge's cold and warm render timings in the proof section.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/ui/html.asl#" :text "Typed markup: Node and Attr enums, one constructor per element the site uses, and a serializer that escapes every text and attribute value, so no source file holds markup in a string.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/ui/html.asl#render" :text "Serializes a Node to HTML: text and attribute values escaped, style and script children written raw, an element with a void name and no children self-closed.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/ui/html.asl#renderDocument" :text "A doctype followed by render of the root node.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/ui/css.asl#" :text "Styles as data: Rule (a selector block or an @media block) and Decl, rendered to a stylesheet.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/ui/bridge.asl#" :text "The op protocol between site.wasm and the DOM bridge: each Op prints as one ASN form per line (:attr :text :swap :copy :store :after).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/ui/markdown.asl#" :text "The Markdown subset the blog uses (headings, fences, tables, lists, quotes, rules, code, strong, emphasis and links) parsed into Nodes; raw HTML stays text.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/app/theme.asl#" :text "The design system: one palette table of colour roles with dark and light values, emitted as custom properties for both themes, and every rule of site.css.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/app/msg.asl#" :text "The messages a click can send and their integer codes, carried in data-msg attributes.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/app/layout.asl#" :text "Routes, the document head, the top bar, the footer and the section header primitives every page is assembled from.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/app/home.asl#" :text "The landing page: the problem, what the language removes, the wire frame, the toolbelt and the proof that the page itself is an ASL program.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/app/docs.asl#" :text "The language on one page, drawn from llms.txt and the README.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/app/blog.asl#" :text "The Post record, the blog index, an article page and the 404 page.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/app/update.asl#" :text "The pure update: the model is an Int64 whose bit 0 is the light theme and bit 1 an explicit choice; step maps a message and the model to the next model and the bridge ops to apply.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/tools/build.asl#" :text "Builds web/dist: copies web/public and the bridge, compiles web/site/main.asl through asl-target-llvm to site.wasm with llc and wasm-ld and plain-named exports, then prerenders every page, site.css, 404.html, sitemap.xml and rss.xml on the host.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/tools/posts.asl#" :text "Reads web/content/posts.asn with asl-parser/reader into published Posts, newest first.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/tools/feeds.asl#" :text "sitemap.xml and rss.xml rendered from the routes and posts through the same Node serializer.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/tests/siteTest.asl#" :text "Serializer escaping, CSS rendering, the bridge encoding, the update transitions and the prerendered home document.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/tests/markdownTest.asl#" :text "The Markdown subset: inline spans, headings, lists, fences, tables, emphasis and escaping.")
